    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for a high-ceiling performance today against a series of vulnerable rotations, headlined by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (71.52) and **Gunnar Henderson** (70.59). **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** draws a favorable park adjustment that offsets a slight platoon disadvantage against Chris Bassitt, while **Gunnar Henderson** utilizes an elite matchup against Corbin to drive significant value despite the expected dynamic platoon dampener. **Sam Antonacci** remains a critical component of our efficiency strategy; batting leadoff against Woods Richardson (4.89 xERA) gives him the highest positional score of the day (67.67) due to his exceptional xwOBA and high-leverage lineup slot.\n\nThe decision to bench **Miguel Vargas** (60.61) was the most difficult call of the morning. While he holds a \"Strong\" daily efficiency score, he ultimately fell short of our top-five threshold as the upside provided by **Coby Mayo** (65.57) and his significant park-factor boost against Corbin proved more compelling. **Coby Mayo** benefits from a dynamic platoon advantage that pushes his base projection into elite territory. Meanwhile, **Dominic Smith** was never a serious contender for the starting five, failing to crack the 40.0 floor due to a poor platoon matchup against Tolle and a low-leverage spot at the bottom of the order.\n\nManagement remains cautious regarding the overall game cap management. While we are aggressively targeting the soft xERA marks presented by Corbin and Woods Richardson, we must remain vigilant regarding the risk of late-inning defensive substitutions if the Waves secure an early lead. With **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Kyle Tucker** both unavailable due to injury or scheduling, the current configuration of **Sam Antonacci**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Josh Jung**, and **Coby Mayo** represents our most stable path to maximizing both counting stats and the scarce stolen base category.",
